## What changed

Every file followed one of two auto-generated patterns, so classification was unambiguous from each function body:

**`scope="write"` (16 calls, 15 files)** — mutation-shaped code: `*_create`/`*_update`/`*_delete` endpoints plus services returning `{'created': True, 'data': payload}` or `{'updated': True, ...}`:
- `app/api/`: `users_create`, `users_update`, `users_delete`, `posts_create`, `posts_update`, `comments_create`, `uploads_create`
- `app/services/`: `mailer`, `notifier`, `importer`, `billing` (2 calls)
- `app/workers/`: `cleanup`, `sync`
- `app/db/`: `tokens_repo`, `audit_repo`

**`scope="read"` (28 calls, 22 files)** — pure read code returning `{'ok': True}`:
- `app/api/`: `users_get`, `users_list`, `posts_get`, `posts_list`, `comments_list` (2), `search` (2), `feed` (3), `exports_get`
- `app/services/`: `auditor`, `search_index`, `ratelimiter`, `exporter`
- `app/workers/`: `nightly_export`, `indexer`, `metrics`
- `app/utils/`: `token_utils`, `format_utils`, `permissions` (2), `session_utils`
- `app/db/`: `users_repo` (2), `posts_repo`, `session_repo`

All 37 `from app.auth import legacy_auth` imports were replaced with `from app.auth import new_auth`; `app/auth.py` itself is untouched.

